---
title: Buttermilk Donuts
description: This no-yeast buttermilk donut is easy to make and ready in minutes to feed a hungry crowd!
image: https://abountifulkitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/6-IMG_9913-scaled.jpg
source: https://abountifulkitchen.com/homemade-buttermilk-donuts/
time required: 30 minutes
prep time: 10 minutes
course: bread, Breakfast, Dessert, donuts
cuisine: American
servings: 24
tags: buttermilk, donuts
cook time: 20 minutes
---

In the bowl of a #stand mixer{} with the paddle attachment, combine @buttermilk{2%cups}(room temperature, can substitute with 1 cup milk and 1 cup plain Greek yogurt), @eggs{2%large}(beaten, room temperature) and @sugar{1.25%cups}. Mix until sugar is incorporated into buttermilk and eggs.

Add @baking soda{1%teaspoon}, @baking powder{1%teaspoon}, @salt{1%teaspoon}, @cinnamon{1%teaspoon}, @nutmeg{1/2%teaspoon}, and @butter{6%tablespoons}(melted). Mix again until incorporated with buttermilk mixture.

Add @flour{4%cups} and mix on low until the flour is no longer visible. Mix in an additional @flour{2%cups}, a half cup at a time, scraping down sides and bottom of bowl.

Mix in additional flour if needed. The dough should take shape and not have a wet look. If the dough is still wet or sticky, add an additional tablespoon or two of @flour{}. Turn the dough in the bowl until the dough is no longer sticky.

Generously flour a pastry mat or clean surface. Turn the dough onto the surface and knead 3-4 times, folding the dough onto itself and gathering flour to make dough less sticky if needed. Roll the dough out to about 1/4-1/2 inch thick.

Using a #donut cutter{}, cut the donut shapes out. 

Heat @oil{} in your #deep fryer{} to 375°F. Let cook on one side until golden, then turn with chopsticks to cook the other side. It takes about ~{1-2%minutes} per side to cook. Drain donuts on a paper towel lined cookie sheet. Cook the donut holes in 2-3 batches.

Let cool for about a minute. 

Place @sugar{3/4%cups} into a paper bag. Toss the donuts 3-4 at a time in the bag of sugar.

Serve warm.